Chapter: IdentityInherit

 A spawned child inherits the parent's identity words. The parent
 declares Identity (for its sets) and Concurrent (for the spawn). The
 child reads its inherited words, which is Identity too -- and the
 capability word it inherits is what lets the read succeed.

Section: Body
  child-body : Integer -> [Identity] Integer
  child-body (x) =
    if identity-whoami 0 == 42 then
      if identity-whoami 1 == 99 then poke-byte 28000 0 1
      else poke-byte 28000 0 2
    else poke-byte 28000 0 3

  finish : Integer -> Text
  finish (pid) =
    let wt = process-wait pid
    in if peek-byte 28000 0 == 1 then "PASS: child inherited identity"
    else "FAIL: child did not inherit"

  step-b : Integer -> [Concurrent] Text
  step-b (s1) = finish (process-spawn (\y -> child-body y))

  step-a : Integer -> [Identity, Concurrent] Text
  step-a (s0) = step-b (identity-set 1 99)

  run-inherit : Integer -> [Identity, Concurrent] Text
  run-inherit (x) = step-a (identity-set 0 42)

  opening : [Console, Identity, Concurrent] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (run-inherit 0)
  end
